msgid "General hints - frequently asked questions"
msgstr "一般提示 - 常见问题"

msgid ""
"Molpro users should have a basic knowledge of quantum chemistry, from text "
"books as recommended below."
msgstr "Molpro 用户应具备量子化学的基础知识，可参考下文推荐的教科书。"

msgid "Also, a basic knowledge of Linux / macOS is required."
msgstr "此外，还需要具备 Linux / macOS 的基础知识。"

msgid "Text books:"
msgstr "教科书："

msgid ""
"Christopher J. Cramer: Essentials of Computational Chemistry: Theories and "
"Models (Wiley, Chichester, 2004)"
msgstr "Christopher J. Cramer: 计算化学精要：理论与模型（Wiley, Chichester, 2004）"

msgid ""
"W.J. Hehre, L. Radom, P.v.R. Schleyer, and J.A. Pople: Ab initio molecular "
"orbital theory (Wiley, New York, 1986)"
msgstr ""
"W.J. Hehre, L. Radom, P.v.R. Schleyer, 和 J.A. Pople: 从头计算分子轨道理论（Wiley, New "
"York, 1986）"

msgid "In a nutshell: how to start"
msgstr "简而言之：如何开始"

msgid ""
"After being familiar with these methods, one may explore more sophisticated "
"tools which rely on them."
msgstr "熟悉这些方法后，可以探索依赖于它们的更复杂的工具。"

msgid "DFT is in many parts similar to Hartree-Fock concerning the input."
msgstr "在输入方面，DFT 在许多部分与 Hartree-Fock 相似。"

msgid ""
"One should start with a basic input and then gradually increase complexity; "
"it is not a good idea to start with a complicated input and then change "
"input parameters without any knowledge what these parameters are meant for. "
"Break problems into small pieces, and try to solve the smaller problems."
msgstr ""
"应当从一个基本的输入开始，然后逐步增加复杂度；从一个复杂的输入开始，然后在不知道这些参数用途的情况下更改输入参数，这不是一个好主意。将问题分解成小块，并尝试解决这些小问题。"

msgid ""
"Introductory `lecture notes <https://www.cond-"
"mat.de/events/correl21/manuscripts/doll.pdf>`__ and corresponding `slides "
"<https://www.cond-mat.de/events/correl21/talks/doll.pdf>`__ from an autumn "
"school in Jülich."
msgstr ""
"来自于利希秋季学校的入门 `讲义 <https://www.cond-"
"mat.de/events/correl21/manuscripts/doll.pdf>`__ 及相应的 `幻灯片 <https://www.cond-"
"mat.de/events/correl21/talks/doll.pdf>`__\\ 。"

msgid "Miscellaneous"
msgstr "杂项"

msgid ""
"Computational parameters such as tolerances, thresholds have been carefully "
"calibrated. Usually they do not need to be changed."
msgstr "诸如容差、阈值等计算参数已经过仔细校准。通常不需要更改它们。"

msgid ""
"Molpro uses a default memory size `(see here) "
"<general_program_structure.html#memory-allocation>`__ which should be "
"sufficient for small systems. When requesting more memory, it is recommended"
" to first get some experience about the memory necessary, and then request a"
" reasonable amount of memory, and not astronomic memory for small systems."
msgstr ""
"Molpro 使用一个默认的内存大小 `（参见此处） "
"<general_program_structure.html#memoryallocation>`__\\ "
"，这对于小系统应该是足够的。当请求更多内存时，建议首先获取关于所需内存的一些经验，然后请求一个合理的数量，而不是为小系统请求天文数字般的内存。"

msgid "Geometry"
msgstr "几何结构"

msgid ""
"The units have to be correct (Angstrom versus bohr). By default, xyz input "
"is in Angstrom, while z-matrix coordinates are in atomic units."
msgstr "单位必须正确（埃对比玻尔）。默认情况下，XYZ 输入使用埃，而 Z-矩阵坐标使用原子单位。"

msgid ""
"A geometry which strongly deviates from the experimental geometry may cause "
"convergence problems. This may be due to unrealistic bond lengths or angles."
" E.g. breaking a bond may require to change the wave function card or method"
" (remember the text book example of H\\ :sub:`2` with a large bond length, "
"RHF versus UHF)."
msgstr ""
"与实验几何结构严重偏离的几何结构可能导致收敛问题。这可能是由于不现实的键长或键角造成的。例如，断裂一个键可能需要改变波函数卡片或方法（回想教科书上关于 "
"H\\ :sub:`2` 大键长的例子，RHF 对比 UHF）。"

msgid "Basis set"
msgstr "基组"

msgid ""
"The basis set has to be chosen with respect to the method, and with respect "
"to the property to be computed."
msgstr "必须根据方法和要计算的性质来选择基组。"

msgid ""
"Negatively charged atoms need diffuse basis functions. A typical example is "
"a molecule containing oxygen, where oxygen usually becomes negatively "
"charged."
msgstr "带负电的原子需要弥散基函数。一个典型的例子是含有氧的分子，其中氧通常带负电。"

msgid "SCF calculations"
msgstr "SCF 计算"

msgid ""
"Symmetry should be exploited if possible. The calculations are faster, "
"easier to converge, and easier to analyse if symmetry is used."
msgstr "应尽可能利用对称性。使用对称性可以使计算更快、更容易收敛，也更容易分析。"

msgid ""
"It should be checked if the symmetry and spin state is correct. The program "
"attempts to find the ground state configuration from the Aufbau principle, "
"but this may fail and then the wave function symmetry and spin need to be "
"specified using a WF (wave function) directive."
msgstr ""
"应检查对称性和自旋态是否正确。程序会尝试根据奥夫鲍原理寻找基态构型，但这可能会失败，此时需要使用WF（波函数）指令来指定波函数的对称性和自旋。"

msgid ""
"After convergence, especially of difficult cases, it is recommended to check"
" orbitals and populations, possibly visualise orbitals."
msgstr "收敛后，特别是对于困难情况，建议检查轨道和布居数，可能的话可视化轨道。"

msgid "Convergence of energy calculations"
msgstr "能量计算的收敛"

msgid "check the geometry"
msgstr "检查几何结构"

msgid "check the initial orbitals (especially in case of MRCI)"
msgstr "检查初始轨道（特别是在MRCI情况下）"

msgid "check the choice of the active space"
msgstr "检查活性空间的选择"

msgid ""
"See also `here <the_scf_program.html#handling-difficult-cases-when-scf-does-"
"not-converge>`__ for hints how to converge SCF calculations."
msgstr ""
"另请参阅\\ `此处 <the_scf_program.html#handling-difficult-cases-when-scf-does-not-"
"converge>`__\\ 以获取如何收敛SCF计算的提示。"

msgid "MCSCF calculations"
msgstr "MCSCF计算"

msgid ""
"The active space (occ, frozen, closed) has to be chosen carefully. (Nearly) "
"degenerate states and low lying excited states should be included, based on "
"e.g. SCF eigenvalues."
msgstr "必须仔细选择活性空间（占据、冻结、闭壳层）。应包含（近）简并态和低激发态，例如基于SCF本征值。"

msgid "AVAS may help to construct suitable starting orbitals."
msgstr "AVAS可能有助于构建合适的初始轨道。"

msgid ""
"NOEXTRA may be necessary in some cases, e.g. if a previous HF calculation "
"was done with nosym"
msgstr "在某些情况下可能需要NOEXTRA，例如，如果先前的HF计算使用了nosym。"

msgid "MRCI and CASPT2 calculations"
msgstr "MRCI和CASPT2计算"

msgid ""
"The active space has to be reasonably chosen (occ, core, closed); e.g. "
"typically after an MCSCF calculation, an MRCI calculation is followed with "
"the same active space."
msgstr "必须合理选择活性空间（占据、核心、闭壳层）；例如，通常在MCSCF计算之后，会使用相同的活性空间进行MRCI计算。"

msgid ""
"MCSCF and MRCI are not black-box like, and e.g. a visualisation of the MCSCF"
" orbitals will help to set up the active space."
msgstr "MCSCF和MRCI并非黑箱操作，例如，可视化MCSCF轨道将有助于设置活性空间。"

msgid "Limit of 32 active orbitals"
msgstr "32个活性轨道的限制"

msgid ""
"There is a limit of at most 32 active orbitals which is unlikely to be "
"increased in the near future, see `here "
"<https://www.molpro.net/pipermail/molpro-user/2017-June/006959.html>`__. An "
"active space of 32 active orbitals is however quite large, and usually "
"smaller active spaces should be sufficient."
msgstr ""
"活性轨道数量最多限制为32个，在可预见的未来不太可能增加，参见 `此处 "
"<https://www.molpro.net/pipermail/molpro-user/2017-June/006959.html>`__\\ "
"。然而，32个活性轨道的活性空间已经相当大，通常更小的活性空间就足够了。"

msgid ""
"Print all orbital coefficients instead of those which are above the default "
"threshold"
msgstr "打印所有轨道系数，而非仅打印高于默认阈值的系数"

msgid "molpro: No such file or directory"
msgstr "molpro：没有这样的文件或目录"

msgid ""
"After installation, you will usually not be able to call molpro by just "
"typing ``molpro``, and you will get error messages such as e.g. ``No such "
"file or directory`` or ``command not found``. You have to bring ``molpro`` "
"into the path. There are various ways such as setting a symbolic link e.g. "
"from ``$HOME/bin/molpro`` to the installed ``molpro`` or explicity including"
" it in the path. Please use a search engine or a book for such questions "
"about Linux."
msgstr ""
"安装后，通常无法仅通过键入 ``molpro`` 来调用Molpro，并且您会收到诸如 ``No such file or directory`` 或 "
"``command not found`` 之类的错误消息。您需要将 ``molpro`` 添加到路径中。有多种方法，例如设置符号链接（例如从 "
"``$HOME/bin/molpro`` 链接到已安装的 ``molpro``\\ "
"）或显式将其包含在路径中。关于此类Linux问题，请使用搜索引擎或参考相关书籍。"

msgid "Hardware"
msgstr "硬件"

msgid ""
"As an introduction, studying the examples in this manual is recommended. "
"Also, the Molpro forum at `https://groups.google.com/g/molpro-user "
"<https://groups.google.com/g/molpro-user>`__ provides a lot of information. "
"We request to post questions concerning Molpro to this forum."
msgstr ""
"作为入门，建议先学习本手册中的示例。此外，位于 `https://groups.google.com/g/molpro-user "
"<https://groups.google.com/g/molpro-user>`__ 的 Molpro 论坛提供了大量信息。我们请求将与 "
"Molpro 相关的问题发布到该论坛。"

msgid ""
"Szabo and N.S. Ostlund: Modern Quantum Chemistry (McGraw-Hill, New York, "
"1989)"
msgstr ""
"Szabo and N.S. Ostlund: Modern Quantum Chemistry (McGraw-Hill, New York, "
"1989)"

msgid ""
"Helgaker, P. Jørgensen, J. Olsen: Molecular Electronic-Structure Theory "
"(Wiley, Chichester, 2000)"
msgstr ""
"Helgaker, P. Jørgensen, J. Olsen: Molecular Electronic-Structure Theory "
"(Wiley, Chichester, 2000)"

msgid ""
"Jensen: Introduction to Computational Chemistry (Wiley, Chichester, 2017)"
msgstr ""
"Jensen: Introduction to Computational Chemistry (Wiley, Chichester, 2017)"

msgid ""
"Kutzelnigg: Einführung in die Theoretische Chemie (Wiley-VCH, Weinheim, "
"2001)"
msgstr ""
"Kutzelnigg: Einführung in die Theoretische Chemie (Wiley-VCH, Weinheim, "
"2001)"

msgid ""
"Beginners should start with Hartree-Fock (basic theory, set up an input for "
"HF, understanding the wf-card input and so on, try out basis sets, inspect "
"orbitals); then one may: - either pursue single-reference methods such as "
"MP2, CCSD and variants - or progress to MCSCF (MULTI) : wf-card, occ, "
"closed, frozen card etc; then methods such as MRCI"
msgstr ""
"初学者应从 Hartree-Fock 开始（基本理论、为 HF 设置输入、理解 wf-card 输入等、尝试各种基组、检查轨道）；然后可以：- "
"要么研究单参考方法，如 MP2、CCSD 及其变体 - 要么进阶到 MCSCF（MULTI）：wf-card、occ、closed、frozen "
"card 等；然后是 MRCI 等方法"

msgid ""
"A more extended introduction how to use Molpro is in :doc:`this section of "
"the manual <quickstart>`."
msgstr "关于如何使用 Molpro 的更详细入门介绍见 :doc:`本手册的这一节 <quickstart>`\\ 。"

msgid ""
"``gprint,basis,orbitals,civector`` may be inserted so that these data are "
"available in the output file; it however makes the output file larger. Use "
"e.g. ``gprint,orbitals=2`` to print occupied and two lowest virtual orbitals"
msgstr ""
"可以插入 ``gprint,basis,orbitals,civector``\\ ，使这些数据在输出文件中可用；但这会使输出文件变大。使用例如 "
"``gprint,orbitals=2`` 来打印占据轨道和两个最低的虚轨道"

msgid ""
"If any kind of problems in a calculation occurs, it is recommended to "
"visualise the geometry and check it for correctness."
msgstr "如果计算中出现任何类型的问题，建议将几何结构可视化并检查其正确性。"

msgid ""
"After converging a difficult system, it may occasionally be necessary to "
"reorder the orbitals (\"rotate\" command) before performing a subsequent "
"correlation calculation."
msgstr "在使一个困难体系收敛后，有时可能需要在执行后续相关计算之前重新排列轨道（\"rotate\" 命令）。"

msgid ""
"Before increasing the number of iterations to very high values (such as "
"\"maxit,500\") far beyond the default:"
msgstr "在将迭代次数增加到远超默认值的很高数值（例如 \"maxit,500\"）之前："

msgid ""
"When excited states are computed, then the preceding MCSCF should be state "
"averaged, and include the excited states so that the orbitals from which the"
" MRCI starts are reasonable. E.g.  "
"``multi;occ,14,4,9,2;frozen,12,1,6,0;wf,47,1,1;state,3`` may be followed by"
"  ``mrci;occ,14,4,9,2;core,12,1,6,0;wf,47,1,1;state,3;``"
msgstr ""
"计算激发态时，前面的 MCSCF 应进行态平均，并包含激发态，以便 MRCI 起始的轨道是合理的。例如 "
"``multi;occ,14,4,9,2;frozen,12,1,6,0;wf,47,1,1;state,3`` 之后可以接 "
"``mrci;occ,14,4,9,2;core,12,1,6,0;wf,47,1,1;state,3;``"

msgid ""
"use: ``gthresh,thrprint=0`` see "
"[[https://www.molpro.net/manual/doku.php?id=program_control&s[]=thrprint#global_thresholds_gthresh\\|here]]"
msgstr ""
"使用：\\ ``gthresh,thrprint=0`` 见 "
"[[https://www.molpro.net/manual/doku.php?id=program_control&s[]=thrprint#global_thresholds_gthresh\\|此处]]"

msgid "molpro not running"
msgstr "molpro 未运行"

msgid ""
"If molpro is in the path, but not properly running, then ``molpro -v`` may "
"help to get information about what goes wrong."
msgstr "如果 molpro 在路径中，但不能正常运行，则 ``molpro -v`` 可能有助于了解出错的原因。"

msgid ""
"It is recommended to use a computer with large memory (RAM) and large disk; "
"also a large memory bandwidth is advantageous. We can however not recommend "
"a certain vendor or CPU. For CPU benchmarks, `https://www.spec.org "
"<https://www.spec.org>`__  may be useful."
msgstr ""
"建议使用具有大内存（RAM）和大磁盘的计算机；大内存带宽也有利。然而，我们无法推荐特定的供应商或 CPU。对于 CPU 基准测试，\\ "
"`https://www.spec.org <https://www.spec.org>`__ 可能有用。"
